From 0e8c3dcfe7289da9ae8eb51d53c08da0efdea6ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:02:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] physim: LabBundle for declared lab worlds; c53
 fed-vortex bundle recipe, controls and credit-free validation

labbundle.py: a lab world as a PhySim bundle (schema physim-lab-bundle-v1): world files (world file,
labkit modules, observe-only channel module), declaration, apparatus, prepared fields and carry keys
(no pickle), suite, truths and checks, with every file and the implementation (runner, adapter,
devices, scorer and labbundle sources; numpy/scipy versions) hashed into the identities. LabBundle
subclasses Bundle with the interface taskset and evaluation use; open_bundle selects it from the
manifest, and taskset.required_bundle now opens bundles through it. The scorer's single port count
requires as many observed ports as actuators; LabBundle refuses other declarations.

scripts/physim/labworlds/fedvortex_*: c53's fed vortices (noise intensity 0.003, ell 2; om additive,
Y proportional) with ports (om,+), (om,-), (Y,+), (Y,-) and observe-only eat and speed channels; a
prepared state from init(31) at t=580 with device 0 on a pinching rod's neck and device 1 on a
drifting vortex; 15 programs (8 generic, 7 mechanism-targeted); calibration-frozen score groups;
2 truths per case; a 64-member native reference and privileged controls (ignore actions, wrong
geometry, initial persistence, flow off, regrowth off, growth off, decay off, body-uniform gain,
dt-halved null); report and validation through required_bundle, LaboratoryTools and evaluation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
